        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Flux.2 Klein image edit - one picture, no extra references\n\nPick the picture you want to change on the Klein Edit node (click the\nfilename widget, or use its upload button), type what you want in the\nprompt box, and press Run.\n\nTo change only part of the picture, right-click the Klein Edit node ->\nOpen in MaskEditor and paint over the area, then save. Leave it\nunmasked to edit the whole thing.\n\nRepoint the three loaders at your own files before running.\n\nThis example is set up for a distilled Flux.2 Klein checkpoint:\n\n  diffusion model - flux-2-klein-9b.safetensors\n  text encoder    - qwen_3_8b.safetensors  (type: flux2)\n  vae             - flux2-klein-vae.safetensors\n\nIf you run a NON-distilled Flux.2 model instead, raise `steps` on the\nsampler (20-30 is normal) and set `cfg` to something above 1.0."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 41,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        -1180,
        700
      ],
      "size": [
        520,
        560
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 13,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Masking - only ever applies to the picture on this node\n\nThe extra reference pictures cannot be masked. They are there to be\nlooked at, nothing more.\n\n  target_megapixels - how big to make the picture being edited. This\n                      also decides how big your result comes out.\n                      Klein is built for about 1.0\n  ref_megapixels    - the same, for each reference picture. These add\n                      up, so turn this down first (try 0.5) if you run\n                      slow or run out of video memory\n  expand_mask       - grows what you painted outwards. 16 is a good\n                      start; 24-32 for hair, fur and soft edges\n  feather_mask      - softens the mask edge. Matters mostly for the\n                      composite at the end, not for the generation\n  binary_mask       - hard edge, no in-between. Off by default so the\n                      feather survives\n\nThe `debug` output below is a plain-text report of what the node\nactually did - sizes, mask state, every reference socket. Read it\nfirst when something looks wrong."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 42,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        860,
        720
      ],
      "size": [
        400,
        420
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 14,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Why the composite at the end\n\nImage Composite Masked puts the edited area back over the ORIGINAL\npicture, using the same mask. Everything you did not paint is pinned\nto the untouched pixels, so the rest of the picture cannot drift in\ncolour or lose detail on its way through the VAE.\n\nEditing the WHOLE picture (no mask)? Then you do not want this:\nselect the Image Composite Masked node and press Ctrl+B to bypass it.\nWith no mask painted, the mask is all black and the composite would\nhand you back the original unchanged.\n\nThe negative prompt goes through ConditioningZeroOut because Klein is\nguidance-distilled and runs at cfg 1.0, where the negative is ignored\nanyway. If you raise cfg above 1.0, swap this for a real prompt."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 43,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        860,
        320
